  "slug": "spiced-butternut-squash-soup-recipe-11998220",
  "name": "Spiced Butternut Squash Soup",
  "recipe_type": "soup",
  "brief_description": "A warm bowl of butternut squash soup is the perfect fall dish. Give it an upgrade with five-spice powder. A popular seasoning in Chinese cuisine, five-spice is a ground mix that often includes anise, cinnamon, cloves, fennel seeds, and Sichuan pepper, in differing amounts.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Combine butternut squash, low-sodium vegetable broth, five-spice powder, garlic powder, salt, and black pepper in a large saucepan. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Reduce heat to medium. Cook, covered, until squash is tender, 10 to 15 minutes. Puree soup in pot with an immersion blender until smooth (or use a potato masher for a chunkier soup). Garnish servings with sour cream and additional five-spice."
    }
  ],
